menu "Build policy"

config KERNEL_FEATURES
    string "Kernel feature override (advanced)"
    default "default"
    help
        Normally leave this at default and use the Kernel submenu. default
        follows kernel/.config (or the architecture defconfig). An explicit
        comma-separated production feature list replaces that feature selection;
        empty disables optional features. Numeric kernel settings remain in
        kernel/.config. Test features are rejected here.

config BOOT_POLICY
    string "Boot policy file"
    default ""
    help
        Optional repository-relative or absolute JSON path with boot-profiles
        and storage-providers. Empty follows the board policy. Runtime policy
        cannot select applications or kernel features.

endmenu
